{
  "0": [
    {
      "text": "A one to ten odd silver coin can cost",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 2.55
    },
    {
      "text": "twice the spot price per ounce.",
      "startSec": 2.55,
      "endSec": 4.9
    },
    {
      "text": "Here is why that happens and when it is",
      "startSec": 4.9,
      "endSec": 6.28
    },
    {
      "text": "worth paying.",
      "startSec": 6.28,
      "endSec": 6.8
    }
  ],
  "1": [
    {
      "text": "Minting a coin costs roughly the same",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 1.8399999999999999
    },
    {
      "text": "whether the coin has 1 troy ounce of",
      "startSec": 1.8399999999999999,
      "endSec": 3.52
    },
    {
      "text": "silver or 1T10O's.",
      "startSec": 3.52,
      "endSec": 5.2
    },
    {
      "text": "Fixed costs spread over 10 times less",
      "startSec": 5.2,
      "endSec": 7.12
    },
    {
      "text": "silver means 10 times the premium per",
      "startSec": 7.12,
      "endSec": 8.94
    },
    {
      "text": "ounce.",
      "startSec": 8.94,
      "endSec": 9.28
    },
    {
      "text": "The silver inside is identical quality",
      "startSec": 9.28,
      "endSec": 11.04
    },
    {
      "text": "at 0.999 fine. You are paying for the",
      "startSec": 11.04,
      "endSec": 13.12
    },
    {
      "text": "denomination, not the metal.",
      "startSec": 13.12,
      "endSec": 14.56
    }
  ],
  "2": [
    {
      "text": "At 32 silver spot, a 1T10oz coin holds",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 3.17
    },
    {
      "text": "320 in silver, dealers charge 650 to 8.",
      "startSec": 3.17,
      "endSec": 6.16
    },
    {
      "text": "That is a 100 to 150% premium over the",
      "startSec": 6.16,
      "endSec": 8.6
    },
    {
      "text": "metal value.",
      "startSec": 8.6,
      "endSec": 9.44
    },
    {
      "text": "That is not a ripoff.",
      "startSec": 9.44,
      "endSec": 10.44
    },
    {
      "text": "That is what the minting economics look",
      "startSec": 10.44,
      "endSec": 11.91
    },
    {
      "text": "like at that denomination.",
      "startSec": 11.91,
      "endSec": 13.04
    },
    {
      "text": "Compare it to a 1oz silver eagle at",
      "startSec": 13.04,
      "endSec": 14.45
    },
    {
      "text": "around 36 for 32 in silver.",
      "startSec": 14.45,
      "endSec": 16.08
    },
    {
      "text": "That is about 12% overspotted.",
      "startSec": 16.08,
      "endSec": 17.48
    }
  ],
  "3": [
    {
      "text": "three sizes cover the market. The 1T10",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 3.12
    },
    {
      "text": "odds is the smallest and most expensive",
      "startSec": 3.12,
      "endSec": 5.2
    },
    {
      "text": "per ounce. The 1/4 odds sits in the",
      "startSec": 5.2,
      "endSec": 7.37
    },
    {
      "text": "middle at around 55% overspot. The 1/2/",
      "startSec": 7.37,
      "endSec": 10.54
    },
    {
      "text": "2 odds is the most",
      "startSec": 10.54,
      "endSec": 11.44
    },
    {
      "text": "efficient fractional option at around",
      "startSec": 11.44,
      "endSec": 13.48
    },
    {
      "text": "25% overspot. All three are 0.999 fine",
      "startSec": 13.48,
      "endSec": 17.04
    },
    {
      "text": "silver from the same",
      "startSec": 17.04,
      "endSec": 17.92
    },
    {
      "text": "mens that produce full ounce coins.",
      "startSec": 17.92,
      "endSec": 21.34
    }
  ],
  "4": [
    {
      "text": "This is what the premium curve looks",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 1.8900000000000001
    },
    {
      "text": "like.",
      "startSec": 1.8900000000000001,
      "endSec": 2.16
    },
    {
      "text": "A one-oz round sits at around 12% over",
      "startSec": 2.16,
      "endSec": 4.62
    },
    {
      "text": "spot.",
      "startSec": 4.62,
      "endSec": 4.96
    },
    {
      "text": "Move down to half-ounce and you hit 25",
      "startSec": 4.96,
      "endSec": 7.19
    },
    {
      "text": "%.",
      "startSec": 7.19,
      "endSec": 7.52
    },
    {
      "text": "Quarter-ounce jumps to 55.",
      "startSec": 7.52,
      "endSec": 9.12
    },
    {
      "text": "The 110-oz can reach 130% or more.",
      "startSec": 9.12,
      "endSec": 11.76
    },
    {
      "text": "Each step down in size adds a",
      "startSec": 11.76,
      "endSec": 13.28
    },
    {
      "text": "significant cost that the silver",
      "startSec": 13.28,
      "endSec": 14.64
    },
    {
      "text": "content itself does not justify.",
      "startSec": 14.64,
      "endSec": 16.32
    },
    {
      "text": "You need a specific reason to pay that",
      "startSec": 16.32,
      "endSec": 18.08
    },
    {
      "text": "premium.",
      "startSec": 18.08,
      "endSec": 18.72
    }
  ],
  "5": [
    {
      "text": "The premium is real, but so is the use",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 2.45
    },
    {
      "text": "case.",
      "startSec": 2.45,
      "endSec": 2.88
    },
    {
      "text": "A full 1-oz coin at 32 and silver",
      "startSec": 2.88,
      "endSec": 5.48
    },
    {
      "text": "creates a change problem in any direct",
      "startSec": 5.48,
      "endSec": 7.03
    },
    {
      "text": "exchange.",
      "startSec": 7.03,
      "endSec": 7.68
    },
    {
      "text": "You cannot break it.",
      "startSec": 7.68,
      "endSec": 8.88
    },
    {
      "text": "A 1T-teen-oz coin at 320 and silver",
      "startSec": 8.88,
      "endSec": 11.04
    },
    {
      "text": "covers a practical range of small",
      "startSec": 11.04,
      "endSec": 12.4
    },
    {
      "text": "transactions",
      "startSec": 12.4,
      "endSec": 12.96
    },
    {
      "text": "without the need to make change.",
      "startSec": 12.96,
      "endSec": 14.32
    },
    {
      "text": "Holding 10 to 20 fractional coins is a",
      "startSec": 14.32,
      "endSec": 16
    },
    {
      "text": "dedicated barter reserve",
      "startSec": 16,
      "endSec": 17.04
    },
    {
      "text": "as a common approach for stacks built",
      "startSec": 17.04,
      "endSec": 18.62
    },
    {
      "text": "primarily in full-ounce form.",
      "startSec": 18.62,
      "endSec": 20
    }
  ],
  "6": [
    {
      "text": "The original United States Mint capsule",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 1.8599999999999999
    },
    {
      "text": ", the familiar Eagle design, and the 6-",
      "startSec": 1.8599999999999999,
      "endSec": 3.81
    },
    {
      "text": "10 price",
      "startSec": 3.81,
      "endSec": 4.32
    },
    {
      "text": "point make the 110 odds silver eagle a",
      "startSec": 4.32,
      "endSec": 6.67
    },
    {
      "text": "natural gift. You are not buying silver",
      "startSec": 6.67,
      "endSec": 8.48
    },
    {
      "text": "by the ounce here.",
      "startSec": 8.48,
      "endSec": 9.36
    },
    {
      "text": "You are buying something with",
      "startSec": 9.36,
      "endSec": 10.56
    },
    {
      "text": "presentation value and lasting material",
      "startSec": 10.56,
      "endSec": 12.26
    },
    {
      "text": "worth.",
      "startSec": 12.26,
      "endSec": 12.72
    },
    {
      "text": "The premium cost is irrelevant when you",
      "startSec": 12.72,
      "endSec": 14.19
    },
    {
      "text": "are purchasing utility, not stacking",
      "startSec": 14.19,
      "endSec": 16.06
    },
    {
      "text": "metal.",
      "startSec": 16.06,
      "endSec": 16.8
    }
  ],
  "7": [
    {
      "text": "If you are building a silver position,",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 1.8199999999999998
    },
    {
      "text": "start with one o's rounds from a",
      "startSec": 1.8199999999999998,
      "endSec": 3.2
    },
    {
      "text": "reputable private mint.",
      "startSec": 3.2,
      "endSec": 4.5
    },
    {
      "text": "Premium runs 5 to 12% over spot, that",
      "startSec": 4.5,
      "endSec": 7.08
    },
    {
      "text": "is far cheaper than paying 100% over on",
      "startSec": 7.08,
      "endSec": 8.92
    },
    {
      "text": "fractional coins.",
      "startSec": 8.92,
      "endSec": 9.8
    },
    {
      "text": "Build your base first.",
      "startSec": 9.8,
      "endSec": 11.4
    },
    {
      "text": "Once you have a core position, fraction",
